| Classification | Evidence | Finding |
|---|---|---|
| Shipped | `.brain/projects/observational-memory/build-observations-recall-typesense.svx` | Typesense `observations` index and default observation-first `sessions search` shipped on 2026-07-12. |
| Current | `run-captured.ts`, `session-index.ts`, live `recall`, live `knowledge search` | Accepted Runs now feed `sessions.db` and SQLite critical search. This is a later recovery path, not the old Typesense contract. |
| Current | `observer-dream.sh`, `/tmp/observer-dream.log` | Reflector applies rollups and archives observation pages on a daily LaunchAgent. |
| Stale/broken | `observer-release/.pi/extensions/observer/lib.ts:435-448` | Observer input still queries retired `run_chunks_dev`; cursor has not advanced beyond 2026-07-20. |
| Stale/inconsistent | `sessions.ts:1214-1226` versus `typesense-recall.ts:25-115` | `sessions search` still reads Typesense observations; `recall` reads SQLite critical.db. They are not one retrieval contract. |
| Drift | `/Users/joel/.joelclaw/search/critical.db` metadata | Critical projection is stale, contains a Typesense observations export error, and was built on 2026-08-03. |
| Drift | `~/Code/joelhooks/content-grill` git status | The SOTA workspace split is uncommitted working-tree migration: old root files are deleted and new `apps/`/`packages/` files are untracked. Its architecture is evidence of shape, not a shipped dependency. |
| Drift | `~/.joelclaw/observer-release` git status | Release checkout has modified `bin/observer-tick.sh` and untracked `.brain/tasks/.brain`, `.brain/tasks/.pi`, `BRAIN.md`, and a launch-agent file. Do not treat it as a clean release receipt. |
| Drift | `joelclaw` git status | The working tree has tracked implementation changes plus a large pre-existing untracked observation archive and other files. This audit did not modify or clean them. |

## Uncertainties and limits

- I did not run `joelclaw observations index --rebuild`, because it mutates the serving Typesense collection and the task allows only this asset, the step, and `/tmp` report edits.
- The live Observer pane was not poked. The missing persisted session file referenced by `~/.joelclaw/observer-session.json` and stale family metadata are enough to reject a clean live-runtime claim, but they do not explain every historical page.
- The current critical database was inspected read-only. Its recorded source counts are build-time metadata, not a fresh rebuild.
- The old Inngest `memory/observe-session` function may still be active for explicit `memory/session.ended` events. That path writes `memory_observations`; it is not evidence that accepted Run deltas reach the Brain Observer.

## Proposed decision-ledger line

- [Audit Current Observational Retrieval Against the Shipped Contract](./audit-current-observational-retrieval.svx) — current accepted Runs append to `sessions.db`, the deployed Observer still reads retired `run_chunks_dev`, and retrieval is split between Typesense `sessions search` and SQLite `recall`; move the canonical Effect Schema Observer/Reflector/projection contract to a dedicated repo, keep `joelclaw` as adapter/runtime, and leave `content-grill` as a bounded consumer.

## Scope note

No implementation source or brief was edited. This asset records the current behavior and the ownership recommendation only.
